                    "instruction_vi": "",
                    "passage": "Antibiotics are vital therapeutic agents used to treat bacterial infections. However, improper dosage and over-prescription have led to global antimicrobial resistance (AMR). \n\nWhen antibiotics are taken incorrectly or prematurely discontinued, surviving bacteria develop resistance mechanisms. Clinicians must adhere to strict antibiotic stewardship protocols—ensuring the correct drug, precise dose, and appropriate route of administration (e.g. oral vs. intravenous) are selected based on microbiological culture testing.",
